task: free-cont-stack (channel-per-element-effect-cost, the interpreter half)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-06
branch: feature/free-cont-stack

why: the audit left this as the largest measured gap. Reading a
  buffered channel one element at a time is 209.3us, and the profile
  is 62% effect machinery against 8% channel: runFree 26%, the Async
  handler 15%, allocating Free nodes 13%, resume 8%.

target: runFree (Effects.scala:263) and Free.fold (Free.scala:54) both
  re-associate a left-nested bind by REBUILDING the tree --
  `Bind(Bind(a, f), g) => Bind(a, f(_).flatMap(g))` allocates a fresh
  Bind AND a fresh closure every step. Replace with an explicit
  continuation stack: Bind(inner, f) pushes f and descends. One cons
  cell per bind instead of a node plus a closure, and no re-association
  at all.

how: keep the answer identical -- this is the interpreter every effect
  in the library runs through, so the matrix is the correctness proof,
  and stack safety is the property most at risk (Free exists to be the
  stack-safe encoding). Measure before and after on the elementwise
  lane; the honest number is the one the profile predicted moves.

caveat accepted up front: a heterogeneous continuation stack needs one
  cast. Operator rule stands -- isolate it in one commented place, do
  not spread it.
